        "original_id": "fcf15ba2-0b7d-5694-a0af-e77f718ddeb2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Georgia O'Keeffe\n- Works: Blue (O'Keeffe series)\n- Concepts: monochromatic palette, non-representational watercolor sets\n- Topics: American art, flowers, skyscrapers, New Mexico landscapes\n\nFacts:\n- Georgia Totto O'Keeffe was born on November 15, 1887, and was an American artist.\n- Blue (O'Keeffe series) was one of the sets of watercolors that Georgia O'Keeffe made while exploring a monochromatic palette with designs that were non-representational of specific objects.\n- Georgia O'Keeffe was best known for her paintings of enlarged flowers, New York skyscrapers, and New Mexico landscapes.\n- Georgia O'Keeffe died on March 6, 1986.",
